{title: 475 - Balm in Gilead}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #475 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 475}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C7/Bb]There is a balm in [F/C]Gilead
[Gm/D]To make [F/C]the wounded [C7/Bb]whole;
[C7/Bb]There is a balm in [F/C]Gilead
[F/C]To heal [C7/Bb]the sin-sick [Dm/A]soul.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C7/Bb]Sometimes I feel [F/C]discouraged,
[Gm/D]And think [F/C]my [C7/Bb]work's in [Gm/D]vain,
[C7/Bb]But then the Holy [F/C]Spirit
[F/C]Revives [C7/Bb]my soul [Dm/A]again.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C7/Bb]If you can [Dm/A]not [C7]preach like [F/A]Peter,
[Gm/D]If you [F/C]can not [C7/Bb]pray like [Gm/D]Paul,
[C7/Bb]You can tell [Dm/A]the [C7]love of [F/A]Jesus,
[F/C]And say [C7/Bb]He died [Dm/A]for all.
{end_of_verse}
